    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d616">

                <pb facs="0739" n="679" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg679"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Mr. Olney</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-25"><hi rendition="#italic">October 25,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge, with
                    thanks, the receipt of Mr. Uhl’s note, No. 228, of the 22d instant, in which he
                    informs me that the commanding officer of the revenue steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Corwin</hi> has been directed to proceed, with his
                    command, to Victoria, British Columbia, and report to Rear-Admiral Stephenson or
                    the senior naval officer at that station, for the purpose of giving testimony in
                    regard to the trial of the British sealing schooner <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Shelby.</hi></p>
                <pb facs="0740" n="680" xml:id="pg680"/>
                <p>I have taken steps to obtain early information as to the date which will be fixed
                    upon for the trial of the <hi rendition="#italic">Beatrice</hi>, and I will not
                    fail to communicate further with you in regard to this subject.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian Pauncefote</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
